[instrumental]

[Intro - steady march, forte]
[no slow buildup - the march hits the ground already moving: three bars of staccato vamp in clarinets, saxes and low brass, snare and bass drum locking the stride, crash cymbal punctuating the downbeats]
[timpani striding on tonic and dominant like Indiana himself, confident from the first step]

[Main Theme - Raiders March]
[the famous hook enters on bold trumpets with a pickup: two quick notes rising stepwise - a dotted-eighth and a sixteenth, snapped short]
[hook cell one: two more quick stepping notes, then a LEAP UP A PERFECT FOURTH landing on a long held note - short-short-LOOONG, the hero planting his flag]
[hook cell two: the line drops away and steps back up into a broad sustained note held three beats, then the rising fourth-leap cell fires again, tied across the barline]
[every phrase is the same rhythmic DNA: quick dotted pickup notes snapping into long confident held notes, staccato on the short notes, weight on the long ones]
[second half of the tune answers and climbs higher, bells joining the strutting accompaniment riff underneath]

[B Theme - lyrical strain, first statement]
[trumpets step aside: clarinets, saxes, French horns and trombones sing the lyrical answer strain, legato and tenuto, warm like sunlight breaking through jungle canopy]
[same rhythmic signature turned tender - each bar one long singing note approached by a quick rising pickup, the bass walking in steady quarters underneath]

[B Theme - full statement]
[flutes, oboe and trumpet take the lyrical strain up high, forte, the melody arching stepwise bar by bar]
[the harmony drifts toward darker flat-side colors, ancient temples and hidden chambers, swelling and climbing]
[the line crests on one accented held note, fortissimo - the artifact raised into the light]

[Main Theme - recap, fortissimo]
[the Raiders hook returns at full power, trumpets and upper winds together, the accompaniment now accented and driving, bells doubling on top]
[both phrases of the march at maximum stride, timpani and drums hammering, this is the triumph of adventure]

[Closing Build]
[sudden drop to mezzo-forte: low brass and low reeds take a moving line, tension coiling]
[accented chord hits stack up like a pyramid, forte, each section piling on]

[Finale - stinger]
[fortissimo held chord across the whole band with timpani rolling underneath, tied long]
[then the final rhythmic tag: sharp accented hits - one, a breath, then a quick dotted snap-snap - crash cymbal choked dead on the last hit]
[short and punchy, no fade, the adventure continues tomorrow]
